        "text_en": "The ascending Dhamanis carry sound, touch, form, taste, smell, inhalation, exhalation, yawning, sneezing, laughter, speech, weeping, and similar sensations, sustaining the body. On reaching the heart, they divide into three each, making thirty branches in all. Of these, ten, in pairs, carry Vata, Pitta, Kapha, blood, and Rasa; through eight a person perceives sound, form, taste, and smell; through two he speaks; through two he produces voice; through two he falls asleep; through two he wakes; two more carry tears; in a woman two are connected with the breasts and carry milk, while in a man these same two carry semen through the chest. Thus these thirty branches have been described in detail. Through them everything above the navel is sustained: the abdomen, the flanks, the back, the chest, the shoulders, the neck, and the arms."
