        "text_en": "If the undetached placenta causes distension of the abdomen and constipation, her throat should be rubbed with a finger wrapped in hair; or fumigation of the mouth of the vagina should be performed with seeds of bitter gourd strung on a thread, mustard seeds, or shed snakeskin mixed with pungent oil; or the palms and soles should be smeared with a paste of langali root; or the head should be doused with the milky sap of a large tree; or a paste of kushtha and langali roots should be given to drink with wine or with urine; or a paste of shala root, or of pippali, with wine; or an asthapana enema should be given, made from a mixture of mustard, kushtha, langali, and the milky sap of a large tree with sura ferment; the same oil may also be used for an uttara-basti; or the placenta may be removed by hand, the hand being anointed with oil and its nails cut short."
