        "text_en": "Now we shall set forth the prescription regarding Bhallataka. Taking a ripe fruit, one cuts it into pieces, boils it as a decoction, strains and cools it; it is taken warm each morning on an empty stomach, after coating the palate, tongue and lips with oil; in the afternoon one eats milk, ghee and rice. The dose is increased by one fruit each day up to five, then by five up to seventy, and thereafter decreased in the same way down to one. Having taken a thousand fruits of Bhallataka, the patient is freed from all forms of Kushtha and from piles, becomes strong, and lives a hundred years."
