        "text_en": "Now we shall describe the Arishtas (medicinal wines). Powders of Patha, Chavya, Chitraka, Suradaru, Sariva, Danti, Trivrit and Trikatu — six Palas of each, plus a Kudava of Badara berries and a Kudava of Triphala; these are poured into an earthen vessel, its inside previously coated with a mixture of Pippali, honey and ghee, into which seven Kudavas of water have been poured, half a Kudava of iron scale and one and a half Tulas of molasses are added; all this is sealed tightly and left to ferment for seven nights in a heap of barley straw, after which it is taken in a suitable dose. This Arishta removes Kushtha, Meha, obesity, jaundice and oedema. In the same way Arishtas are prepared with the Shala-sara, Nyagrodhadi and Aragvadhadi groups."
