        "text_en": "Next we shall describe Ayaskriti (iron preparations). Thin plates of strong steel, coated with salts, are heated red-hot over a fire of cow-dung and plunged sixteen times into a decoction of Triphala and Shala heartwood; these same plates, heated red-hot over Khadira coals, are then allowed to cool and ground into the finest powder, filtered through dense cloth. This dose is taken according to one's strength, mixed with ghee and honey; once it is assimilated, a diet free of sour and salty foods is observed, appropriate to the disease. Having thus taken one Tula of this powder, a person becomes free of Kushtha, obesity, oedema, jaundice, insanity and epilepsy, and lives a hundred years; each additional Tula adds a further hundred years of life. In the same way Ayaskriti preparations are described using all the other metals."
