        "text_en": "Special treatment of Mandali snakebite: In the first stage of poisoning from the bite of the Mandali snake, treatment coincides with that of the corresponding stage in the Darvikara (cobra) bite. In the second stage, the agada compound should be given with honey and ghee, and, having induced vomiting in the patient, the above-mentioned medicinal yavagu gruel should be prescribed. In the third stage, after prescribing strong purgatives and vigorous emetics, the appropriate medicinal gruel should be given. In the fourth and fifth stages, treatment coincides with that of the corresponding stages in the Darvikara (cobra) bite. In the sixth stage, medicines of the madhura (kakolyadi) group taken with milk prove effective. In the seventh stage, the antidotal agada compound in the form of avapida (nasal remedy) neutralizes the action of the venom."
