        "text_en": "Vamsha-twag-adi-agada: This agada is prepared from shavings of green bamboo (vamsha-twak), Amalaka, Kapittha, Trikatu, Haimavati, Kushtha, seeds of Karanja, Tagara, and the flowers of Shirisha, ground together with cow's bile. Applied as a plaster, a nasal remedy, or an eye ointment, it destroys the venom of the spider, the mouse, the snake, and any other poisonous insect. Applied as an eye ointment on the eyelids, as a plaster on the navel region, or as a varti (suppository), it removes retention of stool, urine, and Vayu (gas and the like), or of the fetus in the womb. Applied as a nasal remedy or an eye ointment, it proves healing even in such dangerous eye diseases as Kacha, Arman, Kotha, Patala, and Pushpa."
