        "text_en": "Kalyanaka ghrita: The appropriate quantity of ghee, properly prepared with the decoction and kalka of the substances known as Vidanga, Triphala, Danti, Bhadradaru, Harenu, Talishapatra, Manjishtha, Keshara, Utpala, Padmaka, Dadima, the flower of Malati, both kinds of Rajani, both kinds of Sariva, both kinds of Sthira, Priyangu, Tagara, Kushtha, both kinds of Vrihati, Elavaluka, sandalwood, and Gavakshi — is known as Kalyanaka ghrita. The healing power of this ghrita extends to cases of poisoning, grahapasmara (hysteria caused by the influence of malignant planets and asterisms), jaundice, gara-dosha (slow chemical poisoning), dyspnea, poor appetite, fever, and cough. It is recommended for patients suffering from consumption, as well as for men afflicted with deficiency of semen and women afflicted with infertility."
