        "text_en": "Makshika (stinging flies): Flies (makshika) are divided into six kinds: Kantarika, Krishna, Pingalika, Madhulika, Kashayi, and Sthalika. The bite of any of these is accompanied by swelling and burning. The bite of the Sthalika or Kashayi variety, however, is marked by the preceding symptoms as well as an eruption of pustules (pidaka), with further manifestations following afterward."
