        "text_en": "Mashaka (mosquitoes): Mosquitoes (mashaka) are divided into five kinds: Samudra, Parimandala, Hastimashaka, Krishna, and Parvatiya. The bite of a mashaka (mosquito) is characterized by intense itching and swelling of the affected site; the symptoms of the bite of the mountain (parvatiya) mosquito, however, resemble the symptoms of the bite of deadly poisonous insects, and a sting from the tip of its antennae is accompanied by the appearance of pustules (pidaka) with burning and suppuration when scratched with the nails. The characteristic features of the bite of jalauka (leeches), along with the method of treatment, have already been described earlier."
