        "text_en": "Contact with the dead body, feces, or urine of a poisonous animal is accompanied by itching and burning, stinging pain, an eruption of pidakas (pustules), ulcers and kotha, as well as mucous and painful discharge. The skin in this area tends toward suppuration, and the treatment should be the same as for a wound caused by a poisoned arrow."
