        "text_en": "The bite of an insect with strong and acute venom should be treated as a snakebite, and the threefold remedies employed for snakebite, corresponding to the threefold classification of snakes, should also be used in these cases. Measures of warming, application of plasters, and hot fomentation will prove effective in these cases, except when a patient bitten by an insect is found to be in a fainting state due to suppuration and sloughing of tissue at the site of the bite — in such a case all kinds of cleansing measures (emetics, purgatives, and the like) and antidotal measures should be applied."
