        "text_en": "Now we shall describe the chapter dealing with the pathology of diseases of the sclera (the white coat) of the eye (Shuklagata-roga-vijnaniya). Names: There are, in brief, eleven distinct forms of disease peculiar to the sclera (the white coat) of the eye. Their names are as follows: prastaryarma, shuklarma, kshatarma (raktarma), adhimansarma, snayuvarma, shuktika, arjuna, pishtaka, sira-jala, sira-pidaka, and balasa-grathita."
