        "text_en": "The disease in which small objects can be discerned only with the greatest difficulty even in the daytime, but are seen easily and distinctly at night owing to the weakening of the disturbed Pitta by the cold of the atmosphere (and the general cooling of the earth's surface), is called hrasva-jatya."
