        "text_en": "The form of eye affliction in which the color of the drishti (pupil) of a person afflicted by the doshas resembles the color of a mongoose (and shows an emission of flashes of light resembling it), so that external objects appear multicolored in the daytime, is called nakulindhya. The form of eye affliction, due to the action of disturbed Vayu, in which the drishti (pupil) contracts, becomes deformed, and sinks into the eye socket, accompanied by extreme pain in the affected regions, is called gambhirika."
