        "text_en": "Symptoms when the second patala is affected. False images of gnats, flies, hairs, nets or cobwebs, rings (round spots), flags, and earrings appear to the sight; external objects seem wrapped in mist or haze, as though veiled by a film of water or seen in rain and on overcast days, while multicolored meteors seem to fall incessantly in every direction, when the disturbed doshas are similarly lodged in the second patala (coat) of the drishti. In such cases, the apparent nearness of objects that are actually far off, and the reverse (short-sightedness and long-sightedness), should likewise be attributed to some deficiency in the range of vision (a refractive error in the lens), which deprives the patient of the ability to see clearly and, consequently, to thread a needle."
